orking in consulting actually i  have a phd in astrophysics  okay that's micro might say  well i understood  so what about you what is your  background what did you do before  consulting yes so i always worked in the  retail business and in the consumer  goods business in various firms in  germany and also in other countries um  and i have a fashion and consumer goods  background in that sense so what is your  most memorable moment at inverto so i  think actually at the annual conference  where we were just in france and that  was a great experience to meet everyone  in person after this long cover time and  see how big tall or small everyone was  so not sure if this question really  applies in the current situation but can  you tell us about your most exotic  project location of course so as you  said right now we are a lot in home  office but usually inverto has  projects all over the world and actually  what i what is really nice right now is  that i can be on five continents in one  call so i really enjoy that but of  course i'm also looking forward to  then be on site at the client  [Music]  so i can say at least for myself that  before joining consulting i probably did  not even know what a buying organization  other client would do and for sure also  not what procurement consulting would be  all about so this is exactly what we are  now going to talk about thankfully  daniela prepared a couple of flip charts  for that and will enlighten us so i'd  say let's get over to the meeting room  to dig into it sure  so let's start with the basics what is  procurement and supply chain management  consulting all about  usually we divide it into direct and  indirect articles so direct articles is  everything that flows into the  production of of the article itself that  the that the client produces  so for example if you have a clothing so  it would be everything that is used to  produce this clothing like the buttons  like the fabric and so on  indirect on the other han